{"id": 73, "ts": 1780431859.1327355, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s support for Candidate\u202fC, especially his 100\u202f% reliability and the fact that he consistently creates a positive atmosphere with his crew. Those attributes are essential for long\u2011distance operations where consistency and crew morale are critical. However, his difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric reputation, and lack of willingness to pursue further education raise concerns about his ability to adapt, accept feedback, and maintain effective cockpit communication under stress.\nWhen I compare him with Candidate\u202fB, B handles stress very well and is strong at assessing weather conditions, but his noted grumpiness and uncooperative attitude could undermine crew cooperation just as much. In my view, C\u2019s proven reliability and crew\u2011building strengths still outweigh his communication drawbacks, especially since we have no evidence that B\u2019s stress resilience translates into better overall safety performance.\nTherefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fC, while suggesting we seek additional insight on his feedback orientation and adaptability before finalizing."}
